>As I understand it, the ZLX TURBOchannel framestore has hardware to
>convert 24-bit images to 8-bit dithered images. If so, how is this
>accessed through X? 

Well, no and yes. No ZLX graphics board has a function to convert 24-bit
images to 8-bit dithered images. I suggest using such capable
imaging programs as xv or the Utah raster toolkit. (There are lots
more.) Yes, all ZLX graphics boards do have 8-plane true-color visual
support -- perhaps this is what you are thinking about? This support
includes the capability to render both synthetic graphics and image
into the 8-plane true-color images, but this is not accessable
through core X11. The ZLX-E1 has hardware support for dithering.

