	In a previous message regarding the meaning of the AXP
	acronym, this was written:

	> Someone somewhere invented this trademark.  And he had
	> something on his mind at the time.  What was it?

Every now and then CERN hosts a really good talk by DEC employees
explaining some facet of DEC computers.

At one such talk in 1993, the speaker (who gave an excellent talk on
VMSclusters) mentioned that AXP meant nothing.  DEC arrived at this
acronym by conducting some sort of international search into which
three letter acronyms (TLAs) had not yet been trademarked, and from
that list chose one that sounded catchy and marketable.

Hence, AXP means nothing, and it was generated by a method that had
nothing to do with giving it any hidden meaning (according to a DEC
person).  No conspiracy here, just business.

[Note: I seem to recall some sort of contest posted on the net to
provide the AXP acronym with some sort of catchy meaning.  However,
many hedonistic nights have past, and a few too many brain cells have
died, so my memory is fuzzy here.  Does anybody remember more details,
or am I completely wrong on this account?]
