> The terminal server doesn't seem to be issuing CTS flow control unless I
> disable modem control... !!  Like that makes any sense.  Following is the
> port setting I'm currently using... and it WORKS, but fails to disconnect
> (& reset) the modem on port logout.

  This is one of DEC's many idiotic DECserver bugs. Assuming you're running a
recent version of the DECserver load image, you want no flow control and 
modem enabled. Setting no flow control will actually use CTS, while setting
flow control to CTS will disable flow control if modem is enabled. [See, I
told you it was idiotic!]

