In article <pnord.1130402236E@vunews.valpo.edu>, 
    				pnord@exodus.valpo.edu (Paul Nord) writes:
> Can anyone tell me what is causing this error and how I can fix it?
> 
>   $ run michel_fit2
>   %DCL-W-ACTIMAGE, error activating image MICHEL_FIT2
>   -CLI-E-IMGNAME, image file JOSHUA$DKB200:[TDSS.ALIGN_MC]MICHEL_FIT2.EXE;7
>   -SYSTEM-F-VASFULL, virtual address space is full
> 
> 
> I was getting an error that said "-SYSTEM-F-EXQUOTA, system quota exceeded"
> before I increased the "Pgflquo".  Now I get this.
> 
> I tried increasing the PAGEFILE and SWAPFILE size, but that didn't change
> the error.  Do I need to change it more.

        In addition to increasing the size  of the pagefile, you need to
    increase  the  SYSGEN  parameter VIRTUALPAGECNT (and reboot)  to  be
    about the same size as your pagefile.  Furthermore, any one  process
    is  limited to `PGFLQUO' pages of virtual memory (see AUTHORIZE), so
    this needs to be increased  for  any  account  that needs to run the
    problematic program.  Which ever of these is the smallest is the one
    that  hitting you first (although you get a different error  message
    if PGFLQUO is too small).

        Basically you want PGFLQUO  <=  VIRTUALPAGECNT ~= PAGEFILE size.
    Virtualpagecnt can be somewhat bigger than the pagefile, if I recall
    correctly,  because  you get to count both pagefile space  and  real
    memory (not very technical, but that's the idea).

        BTW, there is no need to increase  your SWAPFILE size, it has no
    impact on this problem to first order.

        -Ken
