In article <CwswwK.ov@beaver.cs.washington.edu>, fred@cs.washington.edu (Fred Videon) writes:
>We've got some DEC DAT drives (TLZ 04 & 06) which I'd like to figure
>out how to interface with Macs.  The companies selling the software
>for this sort of thing provide lists of DAT drive mechanisms which
>their software supports, but nowhere in the DEC literature can I find
>any clue about what the drive mechanisms are in these two units.
>
>Can anyone tell me which drive mechanisms DEC used in the TLZ04 and TLZ06?
>

Usually, most PC-type software that speaks to SCSI tape drives asks the drive
about what it's called.  DEC TLZ0n tape drives will respond with something on
the order of:

	DEC      TLZ06

The software isn't looking for what kind of mechanism the drive has.  It's
looking for that string.  Unless the software specifically mentions that it
supports TLZ04/TLZ06, then it probably won't.

