In article <BKORT.94Sep27180234@k12-nis.bbn.com>, bkort@k12-nis.bbn.com (Barry Kort) writes:
|I have PPP installed on a VAXstation 3100 and on a MicroVAX II with the
|DHV-11 Serial Board.  Has anyone successfully operated PPP on either of
|these platforms?

I've never heard of it.  (I'm assuming you're running Ultrix, 'cause
there's no PPP for VMS.)

|There is no RTS/CTS flow control on the VAXstation MMJ serial connector.
|Is there any practical way to operate PPP without RTS/CTS?  If so, how?

Well, PPP is supposed to support XON/XOFF flow control with control
character escaping for data, so why not go that way?  On the other
hand, the MMJ port can only do 9600 bps, so the best you could do
anyway is V.32-reliable but uncompressed, so you probably don't need
any flow control anyway.

|A related question:  If I connect to the VAX via a terminal server,
|I end up on a PTY instead of a TTY, and PPP won't operate on Ultrix
|if you come in on a PTY.  Has anyone solved this problem?  Is there
|some way using LAT to open a loopback connection that comes back in
|on a LAT TTY?

I've done SLIP over a LAT pseudo-terminal in VMS, so I don't see
any theoretical problem here.  Why not patch the PPP code to jump
around the PTY check and see what crashes? :-)

Aaron



