>Hi everybody,
>
>I just got a Maxoptix TMT3-1300, a 1.3GB optical drive (SCSI). As I don't have
>any document for it, I have no idea if standard Ultrix device drivers support this
>drive. I have tried to make a system special file using rz driver, no luck.

Please describe "no luck".  The version of ULTRIX would be useful as
well.

It is a well behaved SCSI-2 disk, then ULTRIX should at boot recognize
it as "RZxx".  It will given a default partition table that looks like:

A =  32,768
B = 131,072
C = entire disk
G = C - ( A + B )

The remaining partitions aren't defined.

If it is a well behaved SCSI-2 tape, then life becomes considerably
more interesting and you may have to add entry to the SCSI device
tables to use it reasonably.  If you're using the SCSI CAM driver
(optional after V4.2A, default after V4.3A), then the file to look
at is /sys/data/cam_data.c.  If you're using the older driver, look
at /sys/data/scsi_data.c.

If it is a well behaved SCSI-2 fish finder or some other random
thing, all bets are off.  If you're using CAM you may be able
to control it using the CAM interface or write your own driver
for it.

If it isn't well behaved...

>
