Gary Whitehead (Gary@stek.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: Has anyone got a list of devices that you can boot a DEC3000/300L 
: running OSF/1 from?

According to the DEC 3000 Model 300 Series AXP Hardware Reference Guide
(EK-PELCN-OG C01), you can boot from fixed or removable disk, tape,
Ethernet using MOR protocol, or Ethernet using bootp protocol. You can
also boot through a Turbochannel device.

Of course, OSF/1 will need to support the boot device to complete the
operating system startup.

If you have a machine, you can see the devices using the console commands

>>>show config (system configuration)
>>>show device (SCSI and Ethernet)
>>>show bootdef_dev (default boot device)

