Kelvin Pine (kelvin@ariel.ucs.unimelb.EDU.AU) wrote:
: Can someone tell me the escape codes to tell a vt100/220 to start and stop
: printing to a locally attached printer so I can have a SCO printer attached to
: a remote vt220 (vt220 emulator under windows).

For a VT220 (and also VT320 and VT420), the following will do what you want:

CSI ? 5 i  autoprint on
CSI ? 4 i  autoprint off

CSI 5 i    printer controller mode on
CSI 4 i    printer controller mode off

In autoprint, characters to terminal are printed at the end of each line.
Autoprint may be turned on from the keyboard as Ctrl-Printscreen. In
controller mode, characters are passed to the printer, but not displayed.

In the above, CSI is either ESC [ (7-bit) or ASCII 155 (9/11) (8-bit),
and the spaces aren't included in the control sequences.

