Check to ensure that the print head carriage isn't bound up.  With the power
off, open the top cover and try to move the print head carriage back and forth. 
If you can't, then you have some type of a mechanical problem.  It's quite
simple and obvious how it works, so it should be easy to tell.  Is the "end of
ribbon" rivet missing from one end of the ribbon, or has the ribbon jumped out
of the 'V' that the rivet would pull on to reverse the ribbon?

If you can move the print head carriage, then you have some problem with the
motor or driver.  The easiest thing to check is to remove the back cover (with
the power off, and unplugged), and check the fuses on the logic board.  Most
likely you have a blown fuse (probably caused by a mechanical bind on the
carriage).


