>Hi:
>	How can I make a virtual disk in a DEC 5000/25 running 
>Ultrix 4.3 ?

Would you mind explaining what you think a virtual disk is?  My
assumption would be you mean a RAM disk, which is to take a part
of virtual or physical memory and put a driver in front it that
makes it act like a disk.  Using physical memory means it won't
have to be paged, but takes away from other things that need
the memory.  Using virtual memory (as the mfs file system on OSF
does) may require it to page and end up running at disks speeds
anyway.

If this is what you mean by virtual disk, then I don't think ULTRIX
has one publically available.  The system itself uses such a
driver for the installation process, but the driver isn't included
with the system.  It was available for internal use once.  It is
possible that some DEC office sold that to a customer as part of some
consulting they offered, but that's just a guess.

