ROFL!!!!

There is a chip called a PAL - strictly it's a relative of the PROM, and
consists of a programable AND matrix followed by a fixed OR matrix (The PROM is
fixed AND followed by programmable OR). So the definition of that type of PAL
is bogus anyway, as the PAL is not totally uncommitted.

That type of PAL has nothing at all to do with the Privileged Architecture
Library of the Alpha as far as I know.

