I can't give you a circuit diagram, but I can give you a quick'n'dirty
method for adjusting your monitor.  These steps really assume
DECstation 3100 commands and procedures, so you'll have to readup on
the console mode for the VAX 3600 and it's video test commands.

Note: all directions will assume you are facing the screen of the
monitor unless explicitly different.

1. shutdown to the system console
2. power off the monitor and remove the back cover.
3. remove the wire mesh on the top of the monitor.
4. There is a board on the left side of the monitor, this is the cyc
   deflection board and the one where you make all geometry
   adjustments.  On the top of the board, about 2" inside the case
   there are three white knobs in line going away from you.  The
   closest one is focus_1, then focus_2, then screen.
5. Now you need to disconnect all but the green signal connector from
   the VR299.
6. Display the cross hatch on the screen using the VAX 3600 console
   commands.
7. Adjust focus_1 for the sharpest vertical lines.  The adjust focus_2
   for the sharpest horizontal lines.
8. ajust the geometry (h_size, v_size, etc) using the adjustsments on
   the left side of the monitor on the same board.
9. repeat step 7.
10. put all the covers back on and hook up the rest of the cables.


A quick note: I don't have my maint manual in front of my face, so I
could have the adjustments for focus_1 and focus_2 and what they
affect backwards.  It should be fairly obvious when you do the actual
adjustments.  Let me know if you have any problems.

John

