Hi!

Congratulations on your purchase ! I too am a great fan of the old 11/750
machine. A few things :

1.) I'm not so sure that it has 24MB of RAM in it. I know the original DEC
    configuration only supported 1MB of RAM , then it was increased to
    8MB with the L0016 memory controller , and 1MB array boards. You will
    notice that there are only 8 memory slots. Nemonix brought out a fancy
    memory controller that supported 4MB Nemonix array boards. However ,
    the total supported configuration was only 15MB. They even brought out
    a "synchronous clock accelerator " that made it go a little faster. I
    actually have one in mine , and yeah , it goes a little faster.

2.) The VMS you are booting from the tu58 is "standalone" VMS , that has
    most of its functionality stripped from it. You will find the only
    command it accepts is BACKUP. Thats why its called standalone BACKUP!

3.) It sounds to me like you need the VMS distribution , and you to get
    the big tape drive attached. Then you could run standalone BACKUP , 
    and get VMS onto one of your disks , and boot from there.

4.) It may well be that one of your disks has VMS on it already. The 
    11/750 has internal boot ROMS that sit on the memory controller , and
    contain a small boot routine for a particular device. The particular
    boot ROM is selected by the front panel switch "BOOt DEVICE" . Try
    it in all its various positions , and see if a disk will boot.


If you have any other problems , please do not hesitate to contact me !


Leon Heinkelein

11/750 Hacker


