|>, but the scan rate is too high, so I can only see a little of the booting.
|>
|>So what is this machine, and what is it worth?
|>Is there somewhere I can get a DEC 19" monitor fixed?
|>Does this machine run VMS or ultrix?  How can I tell easily?

It would help if you could quote the exact model number from the label on
the back of the unit.  Digital sold a number of different models of
"VAXstation 3100", though if that's all yours says on the front, it's
probably a 3100/40, one of the early models.  VAXstations are different
from DECstations; the latter have MIPS processors and run RISC ULTRIX.
VAX ULTRIX is retired - I don't know if it was available for the
VAXstation 3100.  Otherwise it will run VMS.

I would expect that the CPU used in your model is the "CVAX" chipset,
about 3.5VUPS.  You should be able to attach an ANSI terminal to the serial
output connector on back and use that as a console.  There's a small slide
switch somewhere on the back panel which needs to be thrown in order to enable
the terminal as console.
