ANNOUNCING:  PPP-2.1.2 for the DEC Alpha running OSF/1 (version 2.0).

I have ported the ppp-2.1.2 package to run on the DEC Alpha under
OSF/1.  My set-up is a DEC 3000/300 running OSF/1 version 2.0 --- PPP
seems pretty stable with that configuration, but I have no idea how it
works on other configurations (for example, I don't know if it will
work with version 1.3 of OSF/1).  Note that in my distribution I have
only included code that I have changed and debugged.  In particular, I
have NOT ported the "chat" program that normally comes with ppp-2.1.2.

Installing the ppp package requires rebuilding the operating system
and rebooting.  Needless to say, you must have superuser privileges
in order to do this.

How to get it:  The OSF/1 port can be obtained via anonymous ftp from
zaphod.csci.unt.edu (129.120.3.72), as file /pub/ppp-2.1.2-osf.tgz (it's
a gzip'ed tar file).  After unpacking, you should read the README.osf file
in the unpacked directory --- as stated there, I would like everyone who
is using this port to send me e-mail.  Since this is a first release, there
may very well be bugs, and I would like to be able to contact people if
any bugs are found/fixed.  I am *ESPECIALLY* interested in e-mail from
people who get this software running on different configurations (esp.
other versions of OSF/1).


