In article <wilko.778512467@mango.apd.dec.com>, wilko@uucp (Wilko Bulte) writes:

>jean@CAM.ORG (Jean Laganiere) writes:
>
>>I have a Micro Vax II and I try to install Ultrix v4.4.
>>But I have to do a low level format before.
>
>RD54 must be formatted with MDM (microvax diagnostic monitor).

What he said...

>
>>Can I do it with the RADISK utility?

No, but not for the reason below.  MSCP does have a FORMAT command,
but for a long time there was considerable fear of making it available
at the host OS level; it would be too easy to format disks and
lose data.  As a result FORMAT was only available via dianostics.

This may have changed recently, but radisk(8) doesn't have any
options for doing a format.  I also doubt that ULTRIX has an I/O 
control hook into FORMAT.

>
>RADISK is only for RA type disks as far as I know. So things
>like RA81 etc.

Radisk(8) is for MSCP disks and the RD54 is one of those.  You can
use it to scan for bad blocks and clear forced errors.  You can
also force BBR, but the disk controller should do that itself.

>
>I dunno if MDM comes with the machine (??)

Most MicroVAX II systems came with customer diagnostics and the
formatter was included with that.

