Until DEC decides to add host based routing, what it WON'T do is support
my current network configuration without the outlay of some serious
cash. TCP/IP will support my current network configuration just fine.
BTW, Phase/IP isn't a real requirement for me. I'd love to have the RMS
interface so you can use standard VMS commands across the net. I
probably wouldn't pay for it. We don't use any network apps that don't
already support TCP/IP in addition to DECnet. We do have some that don't
support DECnet, which is why we have Multinet in the first place.

>For instance, DEC's implementation will run ANY vendors IP. Multinet's will 
