In article <344d24$6ff@crocus.csv.warwick.ac.uk>, phrje@csv.warwick.ac.uk
(Dr D McK Paul) wrote:

> We have an Alpha 3000/400 running VMS but do not at present gave any printers
> attached. I have found an Apple Laserwriter IIg which can be connected to
> ethernet. Can anyone tell me how to make the two machine talk to each
> other? What do I need to but or find in the line of software to make this
> combination viable?
> 
> Don

Working as a VAR, we put together a system based on VAX running VMS and the
hardware guys bought a bunch of HP Laserjet III printers with postscript
cartridges and a handful of Dataproducts postscript printers.  We were
quite surprised to discover that the combination was incompatible. 
Investigation turned up the fact that the postscript symbiont put out
commands to the printer that the DEC LN03R could handle but which choked
the others.  We were locked in to these printers and had to get custom
modifications to the symbiont to make it compatible with the 'foreign'
printers.  What a pain.  Things might be better now since I see various
printers advertised in DECdirect but you should check to be sure.

